      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can argue that the colonial powers, despite their oppressive nature, introduced essential modern frameworks that these nations inherited. The establishment of railways and telegraphs, for instance, created a unified national market and allowed for centralized administration across vast territories. Furthermore, the introduction of Western legal and bureaucratic systems provided a standardized, albeit biased, structure upon which modern state institutions could eventually be built. These foundational elements, however flawed, were necessary precursors to modern governance.",
